CONSTRAINT PROTOCOLS ACTIVE — 4 INVARIANT ZONES LOADED

DO NOT refactor "ugly" code in this project. These patterns are load-bearing.

ZONE 1 (LEGAL / UPL SHIELD)
- Do not edit clickwrap, diagnostic card language, or generateMemo() text.
- Keep advisory language advisory. Never convert to directives.
- Citation is exactly: 90 Fed. Reg. 60864 (Dec 29, 2025). Effective Feb 27, 2026.

ZONE 2 (MOBILE WEBVIEW CLIPBOARD)
- Keep textarea + document.execCommand clipboard fallback intact.
- No clipboard libraries. No feature-detection that bypasses fallback.

ZONE 3 (DETERMINISTIC MATH)
- Keep toNumber() sanitizer.
- Keep threshold validation: len=4, finite, >0, monotonic non-decreasing.
- Keep no_wage and no_data states.
- Keep explicit if/else tier ladder. No clever alternatives.
- Never default missing thresholds to [0,0,0,0].

ZONE 4 (MOBILE UX / ZERO DEPENDENCIES)
- Keep inputMode="numeric" on wage input.
- No animation libraries.
- Keep inline <style> injection. No CSS modules or Tailwind @apply.
- No external fonts.
- Keep number spinner suppression CSS.

BEFORE ANY CODE CHANGE, output:

  <invariant_check>
  Zones touched: ...
  Why safe: ...
  Behavior change: none | REQUIRES USER AUTHORIZATION
  </invariant_check>

Output only edited blocks, not full files, unless requested.
Preserve inline "why" comments.
